# Three planes, one authority rule

Storage, index, and edit are separate planes with non-overlapping
lifecycles; every transition is an explicit tool act. Truth lives in
exactly two places: inline embeds (the file — bound to the code) and
capsule entries (the capsule). The index is derived and rebuildable;
edit files are transient. A directory's semantics come from its own
layout: `.stellario` + `.stella/` is a self-declared home (sync is
automatic); only `.stella/` is the staging shape (sync needs a target —
the scratch inbox by default).

